#   2. after,  -timeout 30m     -> like-for-like comparison against run 1
#   3. after,  default timeout  -> the literal acceptance criterion
#
# Host-barrier honesty: the orchestrator ruled that any timing overlapping a
# foreign Go/test process is non-evidence. A single check before the run cannot
# show that, because a foreign suite can start at any moment: other spawn
# runners are live on this host. So each timed run is sampled every 5s and the
# distinct set of Go toolchain processes observed is reported with the timing. A
# run whose sampled set contains anything beyond this script's own package is
